# Every version docs/project-context.md claims, bound to the manifest entry that owns it.
#
# That page exists to tell an agent what its training data gets wrong about THIS stack, and it is read
# far more widely than its history suggests: 60 of the 90 installed skills declare it in
# `persistent_facts`, so it is loaded as foundational context at the start of an agent session rather
# than consulted on demand. A stale line there is not documentation rot — it is a false premise handed
# to the agent before it reads any code, asserted with exactly the confidence of a true one.
#
# It is also not hypothetical. Measured over the page's history, FOURTEEN second-column version numbers
# have been corrected, TWELVE of them in one commit (#746 — Mercure 0.7, Node 24, Next.js 16.2.4,
# Tailwind 4.2, Shadcn 4.3, Playwright 1.59, ESLint 10.2, Prettier 3.8 and four more, all wrong at once)
# landing immediately before this registry existed. Prose drifted alongside them and is still ungated,
# so a green here covers the direction with the worst measured record and says nothing about the other.
#
# Format:  <manifest> :: <dotted path> => <token exactly as written on the page>
#          unbound    :: <why nothing can own it> => <token exactly as written on the page>
#
# The token carries its product name on purpose. Binding the bare number would make the staleness
# direction a tautology — "4" appears in any page of prose — so the check would pass over a page that no
# longer mentions Behat at all. The version is the token's last whitespace-separated word.
#
# The gate (make php.lint.project-context) checks four things:
#   - the manifest still starts with the token's version, so a bump that skips the page fails;
#   - the token still appears verbatim on the page, so rewording a cell without touching this file
#     fails rather than leaving a line guarding a claim nobody makes any more;
#   - every version the page's tables claim is covered by a line here, so a claim added to the page
#     with no entry fails instead of passing in silence;
#   - every line here still covers a claim the extraction FINDS. That last one is what keeps the third
#     honest: the not-empty guard fires only at zero claims, so reformatting one table's columns drops
#     that table out of the universe and every other check stays green — measured, a leading column on
#     the PWA table alone takes 33 claims to 18 while the fifteen orphaned lines keep passing, because
#     their tokens are still page TEXT and that is all the staleness leg reads.
#
# "Starts with" is a floor, and only a constraint that HAS a floor is read: `^`, `~`, `>=`, `=`, a bare
# version, and a PARTIAL wildcard (`8.1.*` — a bare `*`, which twelve `ext-*` entries carry, is refused).
# `<`, `>`, `!=` and any union are refused rather than guessed at — the earlier spelling stripped those
# characters as a charlist, which inverted them, and `<2.0` satisfied the claim "2.0" while
# `^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0` satisfied "24" on a container running 26.
#
# The universe is the PAGE's claims, not the manifests' keys: the second column of each table row, on a
# word followed by whitespace and a number. 33 claims over the page at 406 lines, no false positives. A
# claim whose version-bearing word is a bare noun ("bundle 4.0") is unreadable to a reviewer as well as
# to the extractor — rename it on the page rather than teaching the gate to guess.
#
# What a green does NOT prove:
#   - Nothing about the third column of those tables. It is prose, it is where drift keeps landing
#     alongside the numbers, and no cheap check can falsify it — reading the code is the only control.
#     Nor about any prose outside the tables, which is most of the page. Sampled adversarially, that
#     half still held two provable falsehoods after this registry was written.
#   - Nothing about a version glued to its subject by anything but whitespace. `node:26-trixie` and
#     `dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.5` are stated in second columns and are NOT in the universe — and
#     `node:24-alpine -> node:26-trixie` is one of the values #746 had to correct, so the gap covers a
#     value with a drift record. Same for a version in column 1, an HTML table, a `v`-prefixed version,
#     and a cell containing an escaped pipe (`\|`), which the split reads as a cell boundary.
#   - Nothing about a version stated in the page's PROSE rather than in a table cell — the extraction
#     reads table rows only, and a claim moved into a paragraph leaves the universe silently. A markdown
#     table pasted into a fenced code block goes the other way and mints phantom claims, which fails
#     loudly and is the safe direction.
#   - Nothing about an `unbound` line beyond the fact that somebody wrote a reason. The reason is not
#     checked against anything; it is a statement made where a reviewer will see it, not a proof.
#   - Nothing about anything pinned by digest rather than by manifest — Node and the base images. Nor
#     about the fourth pinned image, `postgres:...` in the root `compose.yaml`, which sits outside the
#     `/api` and `/pwa` directories `.github/dependabot.yaml` tracks.
#   - A dotted path cannot address a manifest key that itself contains a dot. None does today. And
#     composer.lock, where a transitive version lives, exposes no STABLE path — its packages are a
#     positional list, so `packages.N.version` resolves and means nothing.

